From dbada7d85ddccd2437ccdf28ed5467ff81f2925d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:21:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-112: one property list -- the DFM list only what
 the grid does not show; the marker jumps to the .dfm line (0.112.0)

WPF's Properties window is one list, each property once. Here the editable grid
(Left, Top, Caption, the font ...) was followed by the DFM list with all of them
again. Now, behind the grid, the DFM list has only the rest ("DFM other
properties": Font.Charset, Glyph.Data, ParentFont for HotPlate's Save button),
open by default (it is the list's "other" part now, nothing repeated); the
grid's rows reach their .dfm line from the property marker's menu ("to the .dfm,
line N"). A component without the grid still gets the whole DFM list.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 188, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (spbSave: the DFM list Font.Charset / Glyph.Data / ParentFont, open; Top's
menu third item = openDfmLine:353; the whole list without the grid: its
categories fold, by name A-Z, the .dfm order Left, Top, Width, Height, Caption).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
